⚡️⚽️ FIFA is reportedly planning to sell more than a 20% stake in a new $20 billion company managing the World Cup’s commercial rights, aiming to raise $4.2 billion from private investors—including a group reportedly led by Kushner’s Thrive Eternal.

The proposal has sparked outrage across Europe. UEFA is reportedly holding emergency talks this week, with some nations discussing a potential World Cup boycott if the plan moves forward.

